# petkit's sources are LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# ⚠️ Without this line a checkout on a machine with core.autocrlf=true — the
# Git for Windows default — writes every file CRLF, gofmt normalises to LF and
# therefore reports all 26 Go files as unformatted, and `make check` cannot
# pass on Windows at all. Measured 2026-09-15 (CLI-012): `gofmt -d` on one file
# was 134 changed lines, every one of them differing only by a trailing \r.
#
# ⚠️ Changing this re-writes the line endings of every tracked file. Do it in a
# commit of its own, the way this one was.

* text=auto eol=lf
